  {
   "xml_index": 27,
   "xml_name": "L06_027_Average Of An Empty List",
   "display_name": "Average Of An Empty List",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Dividing by zero has no answer in mathematics, and in Python it gives a <code>ZeroDivisionError</code>:</p>\n<pre>total = 50\ncount = 0\nprint(total / count)</pre>\n<pre style=\"color:#b3322a\">File &quot;__tester__.python3&quot;, line 3, in &lt;module&gt;\n  print(total / count)\nZeroDivisionError: division by zero</pre>\n<p>The same error comes from <code>//</code> and <code>%</code> with 0 on the right. Whenever you divide by something that <b>can</b> be 0 (such as the length of a list that may be empty), check for it first. (The exact wording of error messages can differ a little between Python versions, but the error type and the line number are what matter.)</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>average(lst)</code>, which should return the average of the integers in <code>lst</code>, rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>. For an empty list it should return <code>0</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>average([2, 3, 4])</code> returns <code>3.0</code> and <code>average([])</code> returns <code>0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code has at least one error. Use Pre-check (free) to see the error message.\n# Fix the code, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef average(lst):\n    total = 0\n    for x in lst:\n        total = total + x\n    return round(total / len(lst), 2)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(average([]))",
