  {
   "xml_index": 28,
   "xml_name": "L06_028_Percentage Of Zero Total",
   "display_name": "Percentage Of Zero Total",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Here is another division that can fail. A percentage is <code>part * 100 / total</code>, and if <code>total</code> is <code>0</code> (for example, a test with no questions), the division fails with a <code>ZeroDivisionError</code>. The fix is the same as before: check the dangerous case first, and return the answer the problem asks for. (The exact wording of error messages can differ a little between Python versions, but the error type and the line number are what matter.)</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>percentage(marks, total)</code>, where <code>marks</code> and <code>total</code> are non-negative integers and <code>marks</code> is never more than <code>total</code>. It should return <code>marks * 100 / total</code> rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>, or <code>0.0</code> when <code>total</code> is 0.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>percentage(45, 50)</code> returns <code>90.0</code> and <code>percentage(0, 0)</code> returns <code>0.0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code has at least one error. Use Pre-check (free) to see the error message.\n# Fix the code, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef percentage(marks, total):\n    return round(marks * 100 / total, 2)\n",
