  {
   "xml_index": 29,
   "xml_name": "L06_029_Loop Counter Never Changes",
   "display_name": "Loop Counter Never Changes",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Some programs have no error at all, yet <b>never finish</b>. The most common cause is a <code>while</code> loop whose condition never becomes <code>False</code>, often because the loop body forgets to change the variable that the condition tests.</p>\n<p>A program that never stops cannot be tested, so after a few seconds it is stopped and you see a message like:</p>\n<pre style=\"color:#b3322a\">***Time limit exceeded ... infinite loop?***</pre>\n<p>When you see this, look at every <code>while</code> loop and ask: <b>what changes inside the loop that will eventually make the condition <code>False</code>?</b></p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> the program below reads a non-negative integer <code>n</code> (int &gt;= 0) and should print the sum of its digits. It uses <code>n % 10</code> to get the last digit and should use <code>n // 10</code> to remove it. Fix it.</p>\n<p>For example, if the input is <code>123</code>, the output is <code>6</code> (because 1 + 2 + 3 = 6).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code has at least one error. Use Pre-check (free) to see the error message.\n# Fix the code, and add a comment saying what you changed.\nn = int(input())\ntotal = 0\nwhile n > 0:\n    total = total + n % 10\nprint(total)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "123",
     "expected": "6",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "5",
     "expected": "5",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "0",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "9999",
     "expected": "36",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "1000",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 30,
   "xml_name": "L06_030_Condition That Never Becomes False",
   "display_name": "Condition That Never Becomes False",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Sometimes the loop variable <b>does</b> change, but it jumps <b>over</b> the value that would stop the loop. A condition like <code>while i != n:</code> stops only if <code>i</code> becomes exactly <code>n</code>. If <code>i</code> goes up in steps of 2, it may never be exactly <code>n</code>.</p>\n<p>Safer conditions use <code>&lt;</code> or <code>&gt;</code> (for example <code>while i &lt; n:</code>), which also stop when the variable goes past the limit.</p>\n<p>Try tracing the loop by hand for a small input where it fails: write down <code>i</code> after each step and see whether the condition ever becomes <code>False</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>sum_odds_below(n)</code>, which should return the sum of the odd numbers <code>1, 3, 5, ...</code> that are <b>less than</b> <code>n</code>, for a positive integer <code>n</code> (int &gt; 0). If there are none (when <code>n</code> is 1), the sum is <code>0</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>sum_odds_below(10)</code> returns <code>25</code> (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 9) and <code>sum_odds_below(7)</code> returns <code>9</code> (1 + 3 + 5).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code has at least one error. Use Pre-check (free) to see the error message.\n# Fix the code, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef sum_odds_below(n):\n    total = 0\n    i = 1\n    while i != n:\n        total = total + i\n        i = i + 2\n    return total\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_odds_below(10))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "25",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_odds_below(7))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "9",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_odds_below(1))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_odds_below(2))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_odds_below(15))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "49",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_odds_below(20))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "100",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 31,
   "xml_name": "L06_031_Recursion Without Base Case",
   "display_name": "Recursion Without Base Case",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>In Lab 5 you learned that every recursive function needs a <b>base case</b>: an input for which it returns an answer directly, without calling itself. Without it, the function calls itself again and again, forever. Python allows only about 1000 calls inside each other, and then stops the program with a <code>RecursionError</code>:</p>\n<pre>def countdown(n):\n    return countdown(n - 1)\n\ncountdown(3)</pre>\n<pre style=\"color:#b3322a\">File &quot;__tester__.python3&quot;, line 2, in countdown\n  return countdown(n - 1)\n[Previous line repeated 996 more times]\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded</pre>\n<p>The traceback is very long (the same line again and again), but only its <b>last line</b> matters. (The exact wording of error messages can differ a little between Python versions, but the error type and the line number are what matter.)</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>factorial(n)</code> for a non-negative integer <code>n</code> (int &gt;= 0). Remember: <code>0! = 1</code>, and <code>n! = n * (n-1)!</code> for <code>n &gt;= 1</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>factorial(5)</code> returns <code>120</code> and <code>factorial(0)</code> returns <code>1</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code has at least one error. Use Pre-check (free) to see the error message.\n# Fix the code, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef factorial(n):\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(factorial(5))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "120",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(factorial(0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(factorial(1))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(factorial(10))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3628800",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(factorial(7))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "5040",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 32,
   "xml_name": "L06_032_Base Case Never Reached",
   "display_name": "Base Case Never Reached",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Having a base case is not enough: the recursive calls must <b>reach</b> it. If each call changes <code>n</code> by 2, a base case <code>n == 0</code> is reached only from even numbers. From an odd number, <code>n</code> goes <code>5, 3, 1, -1, -3, ...</code> and skips 0, so you get a <code>RecursionError</code> again.</p>\n<p>Like with <code>while</code> loops, a base case written with <code>&lt;=</code> or <code>&lt;</code> (for example <code>if n &lt;= 0:</code>) also catches values that jump past the stopping point.</p>\n<p><b>Test with different kinds of input:</b> a program that works for even numbers may fail for odd ones. Always try a few different small inputs.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the recursive function <code>sum_by_twos(n)</code> for a non-negative integer <code>n</code> (int &gt;= 0). It should return <code>n + (n - 2) + (n - 4) + ...</code>, adding only the terms that are more than 0. For <code>n = 0</code> the sum is 0.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>sum_by_twos(5)</code> returns <code>9</code> (5 + 3 + 1) and <code>sum_by_twos(6)</code> returns <code>12</code> (6 + 4 + 2).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code has at least one error. Use Pre-check (free) to see the error message.\n# Fix the code, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef sum_by_twos(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    return n + sum_by_twos(n - 2)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_by_twos(5))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "9",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_by_twos(6))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "12",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_by_twos(0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_by_twos(7))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "16",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sum_by_twos(1))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
