  {
   "xml_index": 36,
   "xml_name": "L06_036_Off By One In Range",
   "display_name": "Off By One In Range",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The last section is about <b>logical errors</b>: the program runs without any error message, but gives the <b>wrong answer</b>. Python cannot help you here, because as far as Python knows, the program is fine. You have to find the mistake yourself. These are the most common and the hardest bugs, so here are three techniques that work:</p>\n<p><b>1. Compare \"expected\" with \"got\".</b> After Pre-check, look at the test table: which inputs give a wrong answer, and how wrong? An answer that is a little too small often means a loop stops one step early.</p>\n<p><b>2. Trace by hand with a small input.</b> Take the smallest input that fails and write a <b>trace table</b>: one row for each loop step, one column for each variable. For example, for this loop:</p>\n<pre>total = 0\nfor i in range(1, 4):\n    total = total + i</pre>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><th>step</th><th>i</th><th>total after the step</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3</td><td>6</td></tr></table>\n<p>(<code>range(1, 4)</code> gives 1, 2, 3: it stops <b>before</b> 4.)</p>\n<p><b>3. Add temporary <code>print</code> lines</b> to see what the program is really doing, for example <code>print(\"i =\", i, \"total =\", total)</code> inside the loop. Run it with Pre-check and read the output. <b>Remove these lines before Check</b>, because the extra output makes the tests fail.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>sum_to_n(n)</code>, which should return <code>1 + 2 + ... + n</code> for a positive integer <code>n</code> (int &gt; 0).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>sum_to_n(4)</code> returns <code>10</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code runs, but gives wrong answers for some valid inputs.\n# Find and fix the bug, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef sum_to_n(n):\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        total = total + i\n    return total\n",
