  {
   "xml_index": 37,
   "xml_name": "L06_037_Order Of Operations",
   "display_name": "Order Of Operations",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Python follows the same <b>order of operations</b> as mathematics: <code>*</code>, <code>/</code>, <code>//</code> and <code>%</code> are done <b>before</b> <code>+</code> and <code>-</code>. So <code>2 + 6 / 2</code> is <code>2 + 3.0 = 5.0</code>, not <code>4.0</code>. Use brackets to make Python add first: <code>(2 + 6) / 2</code> is <code>4.0</code>.</p>\n<p>When a formula gives a wrong number, write the calculation out step by step for one example, <b>in the order Python does it</b>, and compare with what you meant.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>average3(a, b, c)</code>, which should return the average of three integers, rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>average3(3, 6, 9)</code> returns <code>6.0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code runs, but gives wrong answers for some valid inputs.\n# Find and fix the bug, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef average3(a, b, c):\n    return round(a + b + c / 3, 2)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(average3(3, 6, 9))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "6.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(average3(1, 2, 2))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "1.67",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(average3(10, 20, 30))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "20.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(average3(-3, 0, 3))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
