  {
   "xml_index": 39,
   "xml_name": "L06_039_Total Reset Inside Loop",
   "display_name": "Total Reset Inside Loop",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>An <b>accumulator</b> is a variable that collects a result over a loop, such as a running total or a count. It must be set to its starting value <b>once, before the loop</b>. If the starting line is inside the loop, the total is thrown away at every step.</p>\n<p>A trace table shows this kind of bug at once: watch the value of the accumulator from one step to the next. You can also add <code>print(\"x =\", x, \"total =\", total)</code> as the last line inside the loop, Pre-check, and read the output (remove it before Check).</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>total_marks(marks)</code>, which should return the sum of a <b>non-empty</b> list of integer marks.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>total_marks([40, 35, 20])</code> returns <code>95</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code runs, but gives wrong answers for some valid inputs.\n# Find and fix the bug, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef total_marks(marks):\n    for m in marks:\n        total = 0\n        total = total + m\n    return total\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(total_marks([40, 35, 20]))",
