  {
   "xml_index": 41,
   "xml_name": "L06_041_Separate Ifs Instead Of Elif",
   "display_name": "Separate Ifs Instead Of Elif",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>In a chain <code>if ... elif ... elif ... else</code>, <b>only one</b> branch runs: the first one whose condition is <code>True</code>. With separate <code>if</code> statements, <b>every</b> condition is checked, and a later <code>if</code> can overwrite what an earlier one did.</p>\n<p>Trace the code by hand for one input that gives the wrong answer (for example marks = 90): which lines run, and what is stored in the variable after each one?</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>grade(marks)</code>, for an integer <code>marks</code> from 0 to 100. It should return:</p>\n<ul><li><code>\"A\"</code> for 80 or more,</li><li><code>\"B\"</code> for 60 to 79,</li><li><code>\"C\"</code> for 40 to 59,</li><li><code>\"F\"</code> for less than 40.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, <code>grade(90)</code> returns <code>\"A\"</code> (so <code>print(grade(90))</code> prints <code>A</code>).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code runs, but gives wrong answers for some valid inputs.\n# Find and fix the bug, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef grade(marks):\n    if marks >= 80:\n        g = \"A\"\n    if marks >= 60:\n        g = \"B\"\n    if marks >= 40:\n        g = \"C\"\n    else:\n        g = \"F\"\n    return g\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(grade(90))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "A",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(grade(65))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "B",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(grade(40))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "C",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(grade(39))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "F",
     "extra": "",
