   "xml_name": "L06_043_Boundary Value",
   "display_name": "Boundary Value",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>From here on, the questions work like the debugging questions in exams: the code <b>passes the example test</b>, so Pre-check alone will not show the bug. The bug appears only for some other inputs, which are checked by hidden tests. Read the code carefully, think of <b>corner cases</b> (boundaries, the first and last items, negative numbers, odd and even values) and test them yourself by adding a <code>print(...)</code> call below the function (remove it before Check).</p>\n<p>A classic bug is at the <b>boundary</b>: <code>&gt;</code> versus <code>&gt;=</code>, or <code>&lt;</code> versus <code>&lt;=</code>. The code works for every input except the exact boundary value. Whenever a problem says \"<b>or more</b>\", \"<b>at least</b>\", \"<b>at most</b>\" or \"<b>up to</b>\", test the boundary value itself.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>result(marks)</code>, which should return <code>\"Pass\"</code> if <code>marks</code> is 40 or more, and <code>\"Fail\"</code> otherwise. Inputs your solution must work on: integers from 0 to 100.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>result(75)</code> returns <code>\"Pass\"</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code runs, but gives wrong answers for some valid inputs.\n# Find and fix the bug, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef result(marks):\n    if marks > 40:\n        return \"Pass\"\n    else:\n        return \"Fail\"\n",
