  {
   "xml_index": 44,
   "xml_name": "L06_044_Return Too Early",
   "display_name": "Return Too Early",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>From here on, the questions work like the debugging questions in exams: the code <b>passes the example test</b>, so Pre-check alone will not show the bug. The bug appears only for some other inputs, which are checked by hidden tests. Read the code carefully, think of <b>corner cases</b> (boundaries, the first and last items, negative numbers, odd and even values) and test them yourself by adding a <code>print(...)</code> call below the function (remove it before Check).</p>\n<p><code>return</code> ends the function <b>immediately</b>, even in the middle of a loop. A loop that has <code>return</code> in <b>both</b> the <code>if</code> and the <code>else</code> branch can only ever look at the <b>first</b> item.</p>\n<p>When searching a list, you can answer <code>True</code> as soon as you find the item, but you can answer <code>False</code> only after checking <b>every</b> item, that is, after the loop has finished.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, <code>else</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>contains(lst, x)</code>, which should return <code>True</code> if the integer <code>x</code> is in the list <code>lst</code>, and <code>False</code> otherwise. Do not use the <code>in</code> operator for the search (use a loop). Inputs your solution must work on: any list of integers, including an empty list.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>contains([7, 3, 9], 7)</code> returns <code>True</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# This code runs, but gives wrong answers for some valid inputs.\n# Find and fix the bug, and add a comment saying what you changed.\ndef contains(lst, x):\n    for item in lst:\n        if item == x:\n            return True\n        else:\n            return False\n    return False\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
